      "side": 1,
      "message": "Any of the tests here which reduced in size (e.g. Overflow.asm.frag) demonstrate the principle.\n\nI don\u0027t think we have any good approaches right now for testing codegen that generates less-than-optimal results. For correctness, we have everything in `SkSLTest`, and for checking the raw output we have the output in `/tests/`. But we don\u0027t have a good mechanism for writing a test that detects if SPIR-V emits working code but it contains the same constant twice. If someone breaks this somehow in the future, and the SPIR-V codegen is impacted, the idea is that it will be noticed in the .asm.frag output in code review. (I can see the case for making real pass-fail tests as well, we just don\u0027t have a framework for this today.)",
